618372622178"}, "ownerUsername": "mama_mila_au", "ownerFullName": "Chantel Mila", "history": [{"date": "2026-08-09", "plays": 234568, "likes": 4358, "comments": 9}, {"date": "2026-08-16", "plays": 310709, "likes": 5890, "comments": 16}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "And next time you change your linen, try these tricks. You guys know I start all my linen changes by deodorizing my mattress with one cup of water, one tablespoon of rubbing alcohol, and vanilla oil to leave it smelling so amazing. And you can also use this mix to clean and dust your bedside. When washing your sheets, add one cup of baking soda to the drum to soften and deodorize your linen. Fold your duvet into an S shape, then place a throw underneath to make it look super fluffy, then finish with a candle warmer for ongoing fragrance.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "Education"}, {"shortCode": "DbsLVJKSBKh", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbsLVJKSBKh/", "caption": "Say goodbye to dry cleaning coats with trick #3 \ud83d\ude4c which tip will you try first? \u2764\ufe0f \n1. Hang jeans on felt baby hangers to save space and prevent them slipping off!\n2. Use a soda can tab to double hanging space and keep sets together\n3. If your wool coats smell musty, spray equal parts vodka and water. This helps to remove odours without dry cleaning \n4. Use acrylic shelf dividers to keep folded items neat \n5. Spray perfume on furniture pads to keep clothes smelling fresher for longer \n\nHope these quick tips were helpful lovelies xx \n\n#wardrobeorganisation #capsulewardrobe #wardrobeessentials #tipsandtricks", "timestamp": "2026-08-06T07:29:18.000Z", "videoDuration": 21.106, "videoPlayCount": 290326, "videoViewCount": 126156, "likesCount": 1730, "commentsCount": 17, "displayUrl": "https://scontent-icn2-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/765886912_18103096808190993_7777017896499225764_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_p1080x1080_sh2.08_tt6&_nc_ht=scontent-icn2-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gFcJ